<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-10-30T20:55:37Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Ukraine: Oleshky residents evacuate war-ravaged city</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:39ba6c1fc476bbeeec01084640b4a12405145e1d4b501d93d5fae3c8f419615d</id><updated>2026-10-30T20:55:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T20:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-oleshky-residents-evacuate-war-ravaged-city/a-79812327--58d4dbca74c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-oleshky-residents-evacuate-war-ravaged-city/a-79812327?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Under the local ceasefire, an aid convoy of 25 buses arrived with humanitarian aid and as transport for fleeing Oleshky residents. The Ukrainian city has been occupied by Russia since 2022 and faces food shortages.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Irregular migration from Libya to Crete is rising, raising questions about the links between people smugglers, militias and Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4adcfe7e3e9636610be0c5d11f297255bf8502df211d6607ef52686fbe3840b6</id><updated>2026-10-30T20:55:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T18:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/irregular-migration-from-libya-to-crete-is-rising-raising-questions-about-the-links-between-people-s/a-79808822--583a8979ee7e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/irregular-migration-from-libya-to-crete-is-rising-raising-questions-about-the-links-between-people-smugglers-militias-and-europe/a-79808822?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">There is currently more irregular migration between eastern Libya and Crete, Greece. It's raising questions as to what connects people smugglers with powerful militias in eastern Libya and then in turn, Europeans.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Tennessee woman Christa Pike describes pain after failed execution</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cdfecaf51c20c6bd544b1f8e2fd17941834dd611b113cd05ebf377c52a774328</id><updated>2026-10-30T20:55:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T16:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tennessee-woman-christa-pike-describes-pain-after-failed-execution/a-79810735--d4af8b5b3af1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tennessee-woman-christa-pike-describes-pain-after-failed-execution/a-79810735?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Christa Pike says she remains in constant pain a month after surviving a lethal injection in Tennessee. Her lawyers want her death sentence reduced to life, while the state governor has ordered an investigation.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>What the rift within the Tsikhanouski family means for the Belarusian opposition in exile</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:428d8e1ae83a4b7bef9f4b5549f5c64b8743dd796073b1e8e1e04e5ea0ce02e6</id><updated>2026-10-30T20:55:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T16:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-the-rift-within-the-tsikhanouski-family-means-for-the-belarusian-opposition-in-exile/a-79802776--7fdd2527b18a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-the-rift-within-the-tsikhanouski-family-means-for-the-belarusian-opposition-in-exile/a-79802776?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Siarhei Tsikhanouski criticizes the work of his wife, Sviatlana Tsikhanouskaya, and her office. He also questions her legitimacy. What are the implications for Belarusian political forces in exile?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>US midterms: Pope Leo XIV casts vote by mail</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e0f1ac6c90a846cbafe2293d05964c81556eade56a919129d9c3160dbb5ef688</id><updated>2026-10-30T20:55:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T16:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-midterms-pope-leo-xiv-casts-vote-by-mail/a-79810339--3e151727f070.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-midterms-pope-leo-xiv-casts-vote-by-mail/a-79810339?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As a US citizen, Pope Leo XIV is eligible to vote in US elections and has made use of that right with a postal ballot ahead of Tuesday's midterms. The pontiff, a Chicago native, did not reveal who he voted for.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Binance crypto exchange suspends trades over North Korea-linked hack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fab881663e0ef4c96227227e0140f95394fe67d2dd9e46594396be568e4d4dc5</id><updated>2026-10-30T20:54:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T15:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/binance-crypto-exchange-suspends-trades-over-north-korea-linked-hack/a-79803280--a05325fd4819.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/binance-crypto-exchange-suspends-trades-over-north-korea-linked-hack/a-79803280?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Crypto platform Binance has suspended trading following a suspected hack now linked to North Korea. The disruption has left users unable to trade on the cryptocurrency platform while the suspected breach is investigated.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Merz hopes for Korean reunification at DMZ</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7f25333a721327a5df0f23f7a8d18ff833fac20e8fb80fa1bb41899e86aecc26</id><updated>2026-10-30T20:55:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T14:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-hopes-for-korean-reunification-at-dmz/live-79803462--f2cebaec800e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-hopes-for-korean-reunification-at-dmz/live-79803462?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chancellor Friedrich Merz has expressed hope for Korean reunification during a visit to the heavily fortified border. Meanwhile, President Steinmeier has held talks with China's Xi Jinping in Beijing. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Seoul fears being sidelined as US reaches out to North Korea</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:607b4c1f0443df8635e555717a1d3c2eb4c542c316294797257a0082b035fd47</id><updated>2026-10-30T20:54:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T14:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/seoul-fears-being-sidelined-as-us-reaches-out-to-north-korea/a-79808098--b371be6c550b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/seoul-fears-being-sidelined-as-us-reaches-out-to-north-korea/a-79808098?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With ties between South Korea and the Trump administration strained, the South Korean government worries that Donald Trump's pursuit of a diplomatic breakthrough with Kim Jong Un may come at Seoul's expense.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Bollywood and the underworld — together in the spotlight?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b1dc695ad293543027719d16f0f98846cd2ab1f37c3e64a7db822b478ac38e37</id><updated>2026-10-30T20:54:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T14:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bollywood-and-the-underworld-together-in-the-spotlight/a-79806129--e6b957cc58ac.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bollywood-and-the-underworld-together-in-the-spotlight/a-79806129?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A wave of shootings and extortion threats has rattled India's film industry. This time, those claiming responsibility are very different from the Mumbai underworld that had Bollywood in its grip back in the 1990s.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Bayern Munich's Kenya friendly highlights Africa's growing pull for global sport</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2f82cd6a1ae94e80e27acd7b38eff4a060776f221e17528597e1a69b7d4c66ff</id><updated>2026-10-30T20:54:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T13:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-s-kenya-friendly-highlights-africa-s-growing-pull-for-global-sport/a-79796753--c6f4b50cf1c0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-s-kenya-friendly-highlights-africa-s-growing-pull-for-global-sport/a-79796753?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bayern Munich are to open Nairobi's new Raila Odinga International Stadium against Ajax as Kenya prepares for AFCON 2027. The match highlights Africa's growing sports ambitions — and questions over cost and legacy.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Italy: Students and workers rally over living costs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b2b39cb3cbc8fd026bf7c8a37c91ebfa570b6f9904be1e9247760edd52d6aae</id><updated>2026-10-30T20:54:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T12:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/italy-students-and-workers-rally-over-living-costs/a-79807668--a510f9e16fc0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/italy-students-and-workers-rally-over-living-costs/a-79807668?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Students and workers have marched across Italy for more school funding and relief from rising living costs. The rallies follow weeks of school occupations and protests against higher military spending.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany takes cautious approach on Israeli election results</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ff369bd258cc5298adc5718e237295e8b1ec936da0ec98125b80dad959a545dd</id><updated>2026-10-30T20:54:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T11:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-takes-cautious-approach-on-israeli-election-results/a-79805184--6eb977f23eb2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-takes-cautious-approach-on-israeli-election-results/a-79805184?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German politicians have been slow to respond as they wait to see who is likely to comprise the next coalition. Many are also hoping for a government without religious hardliners.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Russia: Critical newspaper 'Novaya Gazeta' to close</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f042f3f63feb239c10ec8bc44625174752cab4cd1e8f63adbbcb8c6ad5fb1ec5</id><updated>2026-10-30T20:54:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T11:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-critical-newspaper-novaya-gazeta-to-close/a-79805693--37cf795ba96d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-critical-newspaper-novaya-gazeta-to-close/a-79805693?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">"Novaya Gazeta," one of the last remaining independent, critical media outlets in Russia, has announced it is closing under pressure from state authorities. Meanwhile, in Ukraine, evacuations have begun in Oleshky.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil's new anti-gang law: Can it curb organized crime?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c09e2c8b87a9483c8e875f2d318b91db057b84b16b2977ec8bc78ded7689344</id><updated>2026-10-30T20:54:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T11:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brazil-s-new-anti-gang-law-can-it-curb-organized-crime/a-79799450--d75f18b5acf3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brazil-s-new-anti-gang-law-can-it-curb-organized-crime/a-79799450?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A tough stance against organized crime? One year after a massacre that left more than 130 people dead, a new law aims to crack down on drug cartels in Rio's favelas.</summary><category term="NRS-Import" /></entry><entry><title>IIHF ordered to allow Russia back into world championships</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e99ffb0b6ec0eb05e40d4cc37e2ef299f0ca893a755d8461207779892da3da2b</id><updated>2026-10-30T20:54:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T10:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iihf-ordered-to-allow-russia-back-into-world-championships/a-79805650--8e19bd1daa6c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iihf-ordered-to-allow-russia-back-into-world-championships/a-79805650?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Court of Arbitration for Sport has ruled that Russian teams must be allowed to take part in international ice hockey tournaments. The IIHF had banned Russia following the country's full-scale invasion of Ukraine.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Many Turkish 'guest workers' hit by poverty in old age</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ded19c4020e407f2298a1cb7f930119f01dca52f671e2b50e6e45c9ad8f3caa6</id><updated>2026-10-30T20:54:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T08:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/many-turkish-guest-workers-hit-by-poverty-in-old-age/a-79746838--0d5019a9af26.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/many-turkish-guest-workers-hit-by-poverty-in-old-age/a-79746838?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">West Germany and Turkey signed an agreement allowing the temporary recruitment of workers on October 30, 1961. Sixty-five years on, many so-called 'guest workers' can't live from their pensions.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>The dachshund, a humorous icon with political symbolism</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6896d16466b53836e6e1f42232a1ed525c2f91e2f6d29a82d2a62afc93b895e0</id><updated>2026-10-30T20:54:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T07:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-dachshund-a-humorous-icon-with-political-symbolism/a-79640191--0ec0144d606e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-dachshund-a-humorous-icon-with-political-symbolism/a-79640191?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From Picasso to Andy Warhol, a surprising number of artists have portrayed the German breed. But the dachshund has also at times been co-opted as a political symbol.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Space agency to boost GPS alternative with new satellite</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c00267dd7f6ffde07614eeba20c6273416a0946ecc2b2f3ca262f8536c1f0dee</id><updated>2026-10-30T20:54:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T06:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-space-agency-to-boost-gps-alternative-with-new-satellite/live-79803564--d1c7d69799ff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-space-agency-to-boost-gps-alternative-with-new-satellite/live-79803564?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Indian national space agency's mission aims to strengthen its indigenous navigation system and reduce reliance on the US-owned GPS. Meanwhile, Rahul Gandhi renewed his call for more election protests. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli election: Netanyahu, main rival fall short of majority after all votes counted</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b0e8ce2321cbbe273b88f281b9a797d436a8c110b86ec92f171d4e9552556d6d</id><updated>2026-10-30T20:54:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T06:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/israeli-election-netanyahu-main-rival-fall-short-of-majority-after-all-votes-counted/live-79713839--123e742eecd2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/israeli-election-netanyahu-main-rival-fall-short-of-majority-after-all-votes-counted/live-79713839?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With all the votes counted, the pro-Netanyahu bloc finished ahead of Gadi Eisenkot's anti-Netanyahu bloc. But tough coalition talks loom as neither grouping won a majority. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Venezuela: Opposition leader Maria Corina Machado says US backs 2027 election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da2fbfd82873b89b2504258f7f335bb7e5915402bdea4fff445a03f43dbc5c53</id><updated>2026-10-30T20:54:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T03:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/venezuela-opposition-leader-maria-corina-machado-says-us-backs-2027-election/a-79803426--79d168103188.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/venezuela-opposition-leader-maria-corina-machado-says-us-backs-2027-election/a-79803426?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The return of Maria Corina Machado, who says Trump opened the "floodgate to freedom" for Venezuela, presents a challenge for Washington as Trump has also backed interim President Delcy Rodriguez.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bayer wins Roundup cancer trial after Supreme Court ruling</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b38b748de83ff03bdcc9d0bb11bbcf34d8662f71fc42ad03f404ceb88a77dc13</id><updated>2026-10-30T20:54:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T02:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bayer-wins-roundup-cancer-trial-after-supreme-court-ruling/a-79803301--b3d21555ad34.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bayer-wins-roundup-cancer-trial-after-supreme-court-ruling/a-79803301?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The weedkiller Roundup has been accused of being carcinogenic to humans despite no warning on its label. Bayer is seeking to settle tens of thousands of further cases.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
